  "notes": "West's spade opening lead establishes 2 inescapable losers for South. There is nothing to be gained from ducking the first trick so South should win the ♠A in dummy.\n\nSouth has no losers in hearts or diamonds. South must hold his club losers to 1 in order to make the contract. South must hope that East has the ♣A. If West has the ♣A, the defense will always prevail.\n\nSouth may have to lead up to his club holding twice. There are only 2 entries to the dummy, the ♠A and the ♥A. West has just knocked out 1 of them and South must use this entry to make a club play. East ducks and South is allowed to win the trick.\n\nSouth should draw trump ending with dummy's ♥A. A second club is played through East who cannot prevent South from holding his club losers to 1.\n\nIf South had drawn trump immediately after winning the ♠A he would not have sufficient entries to lead clubs twice toward the closed hand. When East ducks the first round of clubs, the contract is defeated since South must then play clubs out of his hand.",
  "commentary_paragraphs": [
    "West's spade opening lead establishes 2 inescapable losers for South. There is nothing to be gained from ducking the first trick so South should win the ♠A in dummy.",
    "South has no losers in hearts or diamonds. South must hold his club losers to 1 in order to make the contract. South must hope that East has the ♣A. If West has the ♣A, the defense will always prevail.",
    "South may have to lead up to his club holding twice. There are only 2 entries to the dummy, the ♠A and the ♥A. West has just knocked out 1 of them and South must use this entry to make a club play. East ducks and South is allowed to win the trick.",
    "South should draw trump ending with dummy's ♥A. A second club is played through East who cannot prevent South from holding his club losers to 1.",
    "If South had drawn trump immediately after winning the ♠A he would not have sufficient entries to lead clubs twice toward the closed hand. When East ducks the first round of clubs, the contract is defeated since South must then play clubs out of his hand."
